# Refactor GCash and PayMaya into Modular Components

This plan refactors the codebase to separate GCash and PayMaya payment flows on both the frontend and backend, making it modular and ready for direct API keys.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend Service Tier

We will create a new payment service structure on the backend to isolate payment platform-specific actions (e.g. creating links, checking statuses, validating transaction details).

#### [NEW] [gcashService.js](file:///c:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/services/payments/gcashService.js)
This service encapsulates GCash direct API integrations (like PayMongo GCash source creation) and AI screenshot verification specific validation checks:
- Boilerplate for PayMongo/Xendit GCash API calls (link generation, source creation).
- GCash transaction reference validation helper.

#### [NEW] [paymayaService.js](file:///c:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/services/payments/paymayaService.js)
This service encapsulates PayMaya/Maya direct API integrations (like Maya Checkout API) and AI screenshot verification specific validation checks:
- Boilerplate for Maya Checkout and Payment Intent API calls.
- PayMaya transaction reference validation helper.

#### [MODIFY] [aiController.js](file:///c:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/controllers/postgres/aiController.js)
- Import `gcashService` and `paymayaService`.
- Delegate platform-specific validation checks to their respective service module inside the receipt verification pipeline.

---

### Frontend Components

We will pull the GCash and PayMaya upload/verification UI out of the monolithic `CheckoutModal.tsx` and place them into clean, separate, reusable components.

#### [NEW] [GCashPayment.tsx](file:///c:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/frontend/src/components/checkout/GCashPayment.tsx)
- Dedicated UI panel for GCash payment.
- Handles GCash-specific design guidelines, branding colors, receipt file input, and loading states.

#### [NEW] [PayMayaPayment.tsx](file:///c:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/frontend/src/components/checkout/PayMayaPayment.tsx)
- Dedicated UI panel for PayMaya (Maya) payment.
- Handles PayMaya-specific green theme branding, receipt file input, and loading states.

#### [MODIFY] [CheckoutModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/frontend/src/components/checkout/CheckoutModal.tsx)
- Clean up the main checkout modal file by importing `<GCashPayment />` and `<PayMayaPayment />`.
- Pass shared handlers (such as `handleFileSelect`, `aiAnalyzing`, `aiVerificationResult`, `paymentVerified`) as props.

